  "step_by_step_reasoning": "1. Identified external user actor (UserConsumerWebMobile) initiating traffic to Route53.\n2. Inbound web traffic flows from Route53 to CloudFront, then to an internal Route53 instance for weighted load balancing.\n3. Internal Route53 splits traffic between two compute stacks: ECS running on Fargate, and API Gateway triggering Lambda functions.\n4. Real-time dynamic weight adjustments are driven by ECS metrics sent to CloudWatch, processed by Lambda (AWS SDK), which updates internal Route53 routing policies.\n5. Both compute paths store and retrieve data across ElastiCache, DocumentDB, RDS, and OpenSearch databases.",
